    rule3Text: "Microwave electric field lines concentrate at sharp corners and edges of rectangular food packages due to dielectric impedance mismatches between the food (ε' = 48-62) and surrounding pressurized water (ε' ≈ 50-70). In high-salinity foods, ionic conductivity increases with temperature, triggering localized thermal runaway where edges exceed 135°C while centers lag at 115°C. High-velocity circulating water must continuously scour package edges to transfer excess surface heat back into the bulk water phase.",
