    rule4Text: "Commercial MATS installations utilize high-power magnetrons or solid-state generators delivering 25 to 600 kW of 915 MHz ISM band radiation. Exposure to 915 MHz radiation penetrates human deep tissue and causes severe internal thermal burns without immediate skin sensations. Under OSHA 1910.97 and FCC Part 18, RF leakage at 5 cm from all waveguide flanges, access doors, and water inlet/outlet tunnels must remain strictly below 5.0 mW/cm² (with commercial alarms set at 1.0 mW/cm²). Waveguides must feature quarter-wavelength reactive chokes and interlocked safety sensors.",
